; The partner plays the top trump. Winning 42 p. 25 (S-0041-a) against Hand
; 30, pp. 102-103 (S-0135-c).
; Rule, in our words: the bidder's partner, following the bidder's trump lead
; and holding the highest trump still out, plays it.
; The book contradicts itself here. Its p. 25 reads a partner's top trump on
; the bidder's lead as his only one (S-0041-a): a partner who follows that
; reading plays low from two or more. Its Hand 30 has the partner play the 6-6
; holding the 6-0 and the 6-1 (S-0135-c), and take the lead to run his
; doubles. This file encodes the worked hand. The reading, as a probability
; over the bidder's worlds, is gates/c02-reading-singleton.silas: 26/57 in
; Hand 30, where it is false; as a fact it needs the partner's policy (GAPS.md,
; policy likelihood).
; Replaces gates/c02-high-trump-handoff.silas. How it differs: it does not;
; the gate was the table's convention, and the worked hand plays it.

(include book)

(policy partner-plays-the-top-trump
  (rule play-the-top-trump (play top)
    (viewer p)
    (bidders-partner p)
    (bidders-lead)
    (trump-led)
    (own-legal top)
    (boss-trump top)))
